  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "46ca0e14-3646-bd17-944f-3365df248a68",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "8c8a5f4e-cc96-e03a-55ba-ddca07348e79",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Nour Festival of Arts.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Over 70 people gathered at Kensington's Leighton House to hear three renowned experts speak on Islamic parks and gardens as vehicles of social change. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The evening's Chair, Philip Wood, introduced fascinating presentations from Jurjen van der Tas: Deputy Director of the Historic Cities Program of the Aga Khan Trust for Culture, Tom Stuart-Smith: ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Internationally-renowned landscape gardener and RHS Chelsea Gold medallist and Mark Bryant: Development Officer for the Centre for the Study of Islam, University of Cardiff.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The ensuing discussion was wide-ranging and included thoughts on how to usefully include traditional Islamic water features in London gardens, to ideas on how to maintain the beauty and tranquility of Al-Azhar Park in Cairo.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
